The pattern of Pascal's triangle is illustrated in the diagram  shown. What is the fourth element in Row 15 of Pascal's triangle? $$
\begin{array}{ccccccccccccc}\vspace{0.1in}
\textrm{Row 0}: & \qquad & & & & & 1 & & & & & & \\ \vspace{0.1in}
\textrm{Row 1}: & \qquad & & & & 1 & & 1 & & & & &\\ \vspace{0.1in}
\textrm{Row 2}: & \qquad & & & 1 & & 2 & & 1 & & & &\\ \vspace{0.1in}
\textrm{Row 3}: & \qquad & & 1 && 3 && 3 && 1&& \\ \vspace{0.1in}
\textrm{Row 4}: & \qquad & 1&& 4 && 6 && 4 && 1
\end{array}
$$

Consider the dark square in an array of unit squares, part of which is shown. The first ring of squares around this center square contains 8 unit squares. The second ring contains 16 unit squares. If we continue this process, then what is the number of unit squares in the $100^{th}$ ring?

[asy]
fill((2,2)--(7,2)--(7,7)--(2,7)--cycle,gray(0.8));
fill((3,3)--(6,3)--(6,6)--(3,6)--cycle,gray(0.6));
fill((4,4)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(5,4)--cycle,black);
for (int i=0; i<10; ++i) {
draw((0,i)--(9,i));
draw((i,0)--(i,9));
}
[/asy]

